# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
.idea/


# verify.py regenerates all three of these on every run -- two from
# out/cv-module.kicad_sch and one from out/cv-module.kicad_pcb. They are KiCad's
# answer about the sheet and the board, not a source of truth, and a stale copy
# in the tree is the one way those comparisons can go quiet without saying so.
out/from-kicad.net
out/from-kicad-erc.json
out/from-kicad-drc.json

# KiCad writes this beside the project when kicad-cli touches it: local UI state,
# not design intent. gen_project.py does not produce it and nothing reads it.
out/cv-module.kicad_prl

# KiCad writes a lock file beside anything it has open. Never committed:
# it names a host and a process, and a stale one makes KiCad refuse a file
# that nothing is holding.
out/~*.lck

# krt.py's routing candidate and its working directory. The candidate is a
# 3.2 MB board KiCadRoutingTools wrote and nobody has accepted yet -- the whole
# point of it not being out/cv-module.kicad_pcb is that a run which produced a
# worse board costs nothing. `--commit` is what promotes one, and what is
# promoted is tracked as the board. The work directory holds the injected
# keep-out geometry and a net-class-flattened project, neither of which is a
# design artefact.
out/cv-module-krt.kicad_pcb
out/krt-work/
# and the siblings kicad-cli leaves beside a board it refills: the DRC report
# it is told to write, and the local UI state it writes uninvited.
out/*.drc.json
out/cv-module-krt.kicad_pro
out/cv-module-krt.kicad_prl
